  def-aqft-threshold-matching-map: formulation-prerequisite
physical_scope: The source-reported one-loop decoupling-subtraction running of the electromagnetic coupling in QED with an electron and a muon; no experimental value, all-orders result, or model-independent threshold claim.
proof_strategy: direct
provenance:
  statement: literature-derived
  proof: ai-generated
sources:
  references:
    - title: C. P. Burgess, Introduction to Effective Field Theory (full review)
      url: https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053
      locator: §4.1.4, equations (81)–(86), the two-flavor QED model, matching at the muon threshold, and the decoupling-subtraction running.
    - title: Aneesh V. Manohar, Introduction to Effective Field Theories (full Les Houches lecture notes)
      url: https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.05863
      locator: Chapter 7, §§7.1–7.2, equations (7.1)–(7.8), the one-loop fermion contribution to QED running and low-energy decoupling.
verification:
  precheck: pending
---

## Example

Use natural units "'$c='"\\hbar=1"'$ and Minkowski signature $'"\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-,+,+,+)"'$. Take QED with a real photon potential $A_'"\\mu"'$, field strength $F_{'"\\mu\\nu}=\\partial_\\mu A_\\nu-\\partial_\\nu A_\\mu"'$, and two Dirac fields $'"\\psi_e,\\psi_\\mu"'$ of charge $-e$ and positive masses $m_e<M_'"\\mu"'$. The covariant derivative is $D_'"\\mu=\\partial_\\mu-ieA_\\mu"'$, and the gauge kinetic term is $-'"\\tfrac14F_{\\mu\\nu}F"'^{'"\\mu\\nu}"'$. Define the dimensionless running coupling by $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(\\mu)=e_{\\mathrm{DS}}(\\mu)"'^2/(4'"\\pi)"'$. The decoupling-subtraction (DS) convention uses minimal subtraction within each interval of active charged fields, removes a charged field from the low-energy theory below its threshold, and matches the coupling continuously at that threshold. Set $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(m_e)=\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}>0"'$ as the low-energy boundary condition. The source-reported one-loop DS flow has two active Dirac fields for $'"\\mu>M_\\mu"'$, one for $m_e<'"\\mu<M_\\mu"'$, and none for $'"\\mu<m_e"'$. If the one-loop solution remains in its positive-coupling domain, then for evaluation scale $Q$,
$$'"\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(Q)}=\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}}-\\frac{1}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{Q"'^2}{m_e''^2}'"\\right)\\qquad(m_e<Q<M_\\mu),"'$$
and
$$'"\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(Q)}=\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}}-\\frac{1}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{M_\\mu"'^2}{m_e''^2}'"\\right)-\\frac{2}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{Q"'^2}{M_'"\\mu"'^2}'"\\right)\\qquad(Q>M_\\mu)."'$$
The two expressions agree continuously at $Q=M_'"\\mu"'$. These are solutions of the supplied one-loop renormalization-group equations; they are not measured values, exact all-orders predictions, or numerical error estimates.

## Example references

[[def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients]]

[[def-aqft-threshold-matching-map]]

[Burgess, full EFT review](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053)

[Manohar, full EFT lecture notes](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.05863)

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The QED field content and conventions in the Example, positive masses $m_e<M_'"\\mu"'$, a positive low-energy coupling $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}"'$, the source-reported piecewise one-loop DS beta equations and boundary conditions, and an evaluation scale $Q$ for which the displayed solution remains positive.

[F1] [[def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients]]: the renormalization scale is an independent positive scale, its logarithm relative to a reference scale is dimensionless, and the coefficient vector follows the supplied beta equation in the declared scheme.

[F2] [[def-aqft-threshold-matching-map]]: the matching map changes the retained field content at a threshold and relates the selected renormalized amplitudes using the same scheme, infrared regulator, and retained truncation.

[F3] [Burgess, full EFT review](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053), §4.1.4, equations (85)–(86): the source reports $'"\\mu"'^2'"\\,d\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}/d\\mu"'^2=2'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}"'^2/(3'"\\pi)"'$ above $M_'"\\mu"'$, $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}"'^2/(3'"\\pi)"'$ between $m_e$ and $M_'"\\mu"'$, and zero below $m_e$, with continuity at $M_'"\\mu"'$ and $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(m_e)=\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}"'$. This is a one-loop perturbative input, not an empirical observation.

[A1] The QED field content and DS threshold convention in the Example are the selected model assumptions. No measured value of either mass or coupling is supplied.

[A2] The one-loop beta equations are used as a truncated source-reported calculation. Higher loops and higher-dimension operators are omitted, with no numerical bound asserted.

## Verification

1.1 On an interval with fixed active-field count $n'"\\in\\{1,2\\}"'$, put $u='"\\log(\\mu"'^2/'"\\mu_*"'^2)$ for any fixed reference scale $'"\\mu_*"'$ in that interval. By [F3], $d'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}/du=n\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}"'^2/(3'"\\pi)"'$. Since $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}>0"'$, differentiation of its reciprocal gives $d(1/'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}})/du=-n/(3\\pi)"'$. Integrating between two scales in this interval yields the corresponding affine function of $'"\\log\\mu"'^2$. [given, F3, A2, algebra]

1.2 Between $m_e$ and $M_'"\\mu"'$, take $n=1$ and use the boundary value $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(m_e)=\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}"'$. Step 1.1 gives
$$'"\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(Q)}=\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}}-\\frac{1}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{Q"'^2}{m_e''^2}'"\\right)"'$$
for $m_e<Q<M_'"\\mu"'$. [F3, A1, step 1.1, algebra]

1.3 At $'"\\mu=M_\\mu"'$, the low-energy value is therefore
$$'"\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(M_\\mu)}=\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}}-\\frac{1}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{M_\\mu"'^2}{m_e''^2}'"\\right)."'$$
The DS boundary condition sets the high-energy coupling equal to this value at the threshold. Above it $n=2$, so integrating step 1.1 from $M_'"\\mu"'$ to $Q$ gives
$$'"\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{DS}}(Q)}=\\frac{1}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}}-\\frac{1}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{M_\\mu"'^2}{m_e''^2}'"\\right)-\\frac{2}{3\\pi}\\log\\"'!'"\\left(\\frac{Q"'^2}{M_'"\\mu"'^2}'"\\right)"'$$
for $Q>M_'"\\mu"'$. [F3, step 1.1, step 1.2, algebra]

1.4 Setting $Q=M_'"\\mu"'$ in the upper expression removes its last logarithm and gives exactly the lower expression at the threshold. Setting $Q=m_e$ in the lower expression recovers $'"\\alpha_{\\mathrm{phys}}"'$. Thus the piecewise one-loop solution satisfies both stated boundary conditions and is continuous at the threshold. [F3, step 1.2, step 1.3, algebra] ∎
