## Sources read for this A page

1. A. V. Manohar, “Introduction to Effective Field Theories,” full 94-page
   Les Houches lecture notes,
   <https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.05863>. Read Chapter 5 §§5.5–5.7 on matching,
   common IR terms, matching-scale choices and RG evolution; §5.10 on
   coefficient evolution and operator mixing; and Chapter 7 §§7.1–7.2 on
   momentum subtraction, QED threshold decoupling and the contrast with MS.
   These passages support the matching/RG conventions and QED example; they
   do not prove the local compatibility theorem or supply a general EFT beta
   matrix.
2. C. P. Burgess, “Introduction to Effective Field Theory,” full 55-page
   review, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053>. Read §§2.2.1–2.2.2 on the
   Wilson action and cancellation of its intermediate-scale dependence, and
   §4.1.4 on electron/muon thresholds, decoupling subtraction, continuous
   threshold matching, and the piecewise one-loop QED beta function. This is
   an independent treatment and full text; it does not establish a universal
   matching theorem or bound omitted EFT terms.

