## Item checkpoint — pthm-aqft-matching-and-running-scale-independence

Authored the conditional finite-order physics theorem. In realified coefficient
coordinates, a continuously differentiable matching map satisfying the
RG-compatibility identity transports every high-energy trajectory to a
low-energy trajectory. Uniqueness then makes the final low-energy coefficient
vector independent of the chosen intermediate matching scale. At the fixed
final scale and fixed external states, kinematics, IR regulator and truncation,
the selected low-energy amplitudes/Green functions therefore agree for every
matching scale. A finite sequence follows by induction. The theorem assumes
flow existence over the stated interval and matching compatibility; it does not
calculate coefficients, infer continuum existence, or assign omitted-order
bounds.

Conventions are those of def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients:
dimensionless logarithmic scale t=log(mu/mu0), finite complex coefficient
vectors with realification, and supplied beta fields. The matching map and
common IR-regulator/truncation meaning are those in
def-aqft-threshold-matching-map. The RG compatibility identity is stated in
realified coordinates so its derivative and beta vector have the same finite
real domains.

Direct dependencies and roles:

- def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients — mathematical-premise.
- def-aqft-threshold-matching-map — formulation-prerequisite.
- thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness — mathematical-premise.

The item has dependency_level 5: one plus the maximum supplier level 4
(threshold map 4, supplied RG well-posedness theorem 4; scheme definition 3).
The actual full proof of thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness was read:
it proves common local solutions under the continuous, locally uniform
state-Lipschitz hypotheses, then proves uniqueness on any common interval.
This consumer assumes the particular full/low trajectories exist on the
declared compact interval, so it does not turn local ODE existence into an
unproved global-flow claim.

