 ex-aqft-qed-threshold-matching def-aqft-threshold-matching-map items/def-aqft-threshold-matching-map.md 'A declared matching calculation supplies a finite list of renormalized amplitudes or Green-function values $A_{\\sigma,j}(t,c;\\lambda_{\\mathrm{IR}})$, where $j$ indexes the selected external states and kinematics, $c$ is a coefficient vector, and $\\lambda_{\\mathrm{IR}}$ denotes the common infrared regulator used in both descriptions. Let $U_\\sigma\\subset\\mathbb C^{N_\\sigma}$ be open coefficient domains for $\\sigma\\in\\{+,-\\}$. The supplied matching family is a jointly continuously differentiable real map $\\widehat{\\mathcal M}:\\mathcal V\\to\\rho_{N_-}(U_-)$ on an open domain $\\mathcal V\\subset J\\times\\rho_{N_+}(U_+)$. Its admissible domain is the open subset $\\mathcal U=\\{(t,x)\\in\\mathcal V:(t,x)\\in\\Omega_+,\\ (t,\\widehat{\\mathcal M}(t,x))\\in\\Omega_-\\}$. It defines $M_t(c):=\\rho_{N_-}^{-1}(\\widehat{\\mathcal M}(t,\\rho_{N_+}(c)))$ for each admitted $(t,c)$, and $\\widehat M_t(x):=\\widehat{\\mathcal M}(t,x)$ on the corresponding slice. Thus the scale derivative and coefficient derivative in the compatibility condition below both exist and are continuous. It is a matching map through the declared loop order, operator dimension, and mass-expansion order when, for every selected $j$ and every admitted pair $(t,c)$ with $c\\in U_+$, the prescribed truncations of $A_{+,j}(t,c;\\lambda_{\\mathrm{IR}})$ and $A_{-,j}(t,M_t(c);\\lambda_{\\mathrm{IR}})$ agree. The truncation projection and its retained orders are part of the datum. This equality records only the selected amplitudes and orders; it neither estimates discarded terms nor asserts that a matching calculation exists for every model.\n\nA matching map is RG-compatible on these domains when, in realified coefficient coordinates,\n$$\\partial_t\\widehat M_t(x)+D_x\\widehat M_t(x)\\,\\beta_+(t,x)=\\beta_-\\!\\left(t,\\widehat M_t(x)\\right)$$\nfor every admitted $(t,x)$. Here $D_x$ is the ordinary real derivative with respect to the coefficient coordinates. RG-compatibility is an additional condition to be checked from the supplied beta functions and matching calculation; it does not follow merely from defining $M_t$ by amplitude equality.'
